{{Quote|After Palpatine, nobody wanted to hand over that much power again, so we don't have an executive, only a chancellor with no real authority. Mon Mothma got things done through sheer charisma, but almost every chancellor since her has been''&hellip;"<br />"''Useless.|Leia Organa and [[Han Solo]]|<ref name="Bloodline">[[Bloodline (novel)|''Bloodline'']]</ref>}}
'''Chancellor''', also known as '''Supreme Chancellor''' or the '''Chief of State''' was the [[Politics|head of state]] of the [[New Republic]]. However a chancellor was not a nominal chief executive and the role was relegated to a ceremonial role with limited authority. Nevertheless, a chancellor possessed certain powers that may be exercised discretionally.

Upon the [[Declaration of a New Republic|formation]] of the New Republic, [[Mon Mothma]] was [[Democracy|elected]]. Due to the position being the [[Charter of Chancellor|legal]] continuation of the position of [[Supreme Chancellor]] under the [[Galactic Republic]], Mothma technically succeeded [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]], but eliminated the [[Emergency Powers Act|emergency]] [[Reflex Amendment|powers]] inherited from her predecessor and was subjected to restrictions that were designed to prevent any chancellor from accruing any real power, and therefore lost control over the [[New Republic Senate|Galactic Senate]]. Mothma's successors maintained this following the end of her term.

However, differing views emerged from two major political factions in the Senate, commonly referred to as the [[Centrists]] and [[Populists]], who disagreed on the extent to which if a [[First Senator|new and more powerful]] title should to replace the chancellor and would have been tasked with bringing order to the divided government, but the debate ended with no consensus and the election for its postponed indefinitely. 

In [[32 ABY]], [[Lanever Villecham]] was elected as the chancellor. A believer in the peace initiatives of the New Republic, Villecham focused his term on improved trade relations with neutral [[star system]]s instead of the [[First Order military|military]] [[Cold War|build-up]] with the [[First Order]], that ended with the [[Hosnian Cataclysm|destruction]] of the [[Hosnian system]], where the chancellor [[death|died]], with the First Order [[First Order-Resistance War|invasion]] of [[the galaxy]] soon realized.

==Powers==
{{Main|Charter of Chancellor}}
{{Quote|The charter of Chancellor maintains the emergency powers granted by Palpatine, and they can persist no longer. They are a poison to democracy. They undercut my role.|Mon Mothma, first chancellor of the New Republic|<ref name="Aftermath" />}}
[[File:TheSenateSquad.jpg|thumb|left|250px|The chancellor was the elected leader of the New Republic.]]
The office of the chancellor would have little central authority,<ref name="Bloodline" /> which became a chancellery with a limited powers similar to that made during the [[Ruusan Reformations]],<ref name="Collapse of the Republic">''[[Collapse of the Republic]]''</ref> and was not even a nominal chief executive,<ref name="Bloodline" /> and was subjected to restrictions that were designed to prevent any chancellor from accruing any real power.<ref name="TSWB" /> The powers of the chancellor themselves were derived from the [[charter of Chancellor]], where chancellery was formally known as Supreme Chancellor and was empowered to be leader of the [[New Republic Senate|Galactic Senate]].<ref name="Aftermath" /> A chancellor would officially represent the New Republic, receiving dignitaries<ref name="Life Debt">''[[Aftermath: Life Debt]]''</ref> and concluding treaties with other governments.<ref name="Empire's End" /> 

The first New Republic chancellor, [[Mon Mothma]], was given the emergency powers that were once granted to [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]] of the [[Galactic Republic]] during the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="Aftermath" /> As someone who had spent the duration of the Clone Wars arguing against the increased powers of the chancellor<ref name="Mothma Databank">{{Databank|mon-mothma|Mon Mothma}}</ref> and eager to distance her new government from that of Palpatine's,<ref name="Who's Boss">{{InsiderCite|224|Who's the Boss?}}</ref> Mothma intended to eliminate the emergency powers from her position. Though the powers granted her the authority to send [[New Republic Defense Force|New Republic forces]] to fight and die wherever she chose, she did not want such a responsibility and felt that it was a poison to [[democracy]]. Instead, she submitted to the will of the Senate, even in military matters such as the disarmament of the [[New Republic Defense Fleet]].<ref name="Aftermath" />

==History==
===Background===
{{Main|Supreme Chancellor|Chancellor (Rebel Alliance)}}
{{Quote|Her first decision seemed like a semantic one, but it really underlined the extent to which Mon Mothma was planning for a decentralized system of power. Where Palpatine had once been the supreme chancellor, she would just be chancellor. "Supreme" had very unwelcome connotations that could have no place in the new galaxy.|Beaumont Kin, The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire|<ref name="Rise and Fall">''[[Star Wars: The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]''</ref>}}
[[File:SenateCrest-TPM.png|thumb|right|250px|The Supreme Chancellor was the head of state and head of government of the Galactic Republic.]]
The origins of the chancellery came from the Galactic Republic,<ref name="Aftermath" /> where the Supreme Chancellor served as the leader of the [[Galactic Senate]] and the [[Politics|head of state]] of the Republic itself. Established by [[Tarsus Valorum]]<ref name="RotS">''[[Rise of the Separatists]]''</ref> who served as the first Supreme Chancellor following the [[fall of the Old Republic]], in which the [[Sith]] were [[Jedi-Sith War|defeated]] by the [[Jedi Order]].<ref name="Tarkin">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref> The power of the Supreme Chancellor would be limited by the Ruusan Reformations.<ref name="Collapse of the Republic">''[[Collapse of the Republic]]''</ref>

During the Clone Wars, Supreme Chancellor Palpatine [[Emergency Powers Act|amassed]] more and more [[Reflex Amendment|executive powers]] until,<ref name="Collapse of the Republic" /> at the end of the war, he had enough power to [[Proclamation of the New Order|transform]] the Republic into the [[Galactic Empire]] and declare himself [[Galactic Emperor|sovereign ruler]] of [[the galaxy]].<ref name="Episode III">{{Film|III}}</ref> 

The position was used by the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]], where former [[senator]] Mon Mothma was given the [[Military rank|rank]] of [[Chancellor (Rebel Alliance)|chancellor]] while serving as the Alliance's civilian leader.<ref name="Star Wars 4">[[Star Wars (2015) 4|''Star Wars'' (2015) 4]]</ref>

===Mon Mothma===
{{Quote|Like the Rebel Alliance before us, like the New Republic now. We persevere.|Mon Mothma|<ref name="Empire's End">''[[Aftermath: Empire's End]]''</ref>}}
[[File:Manybothansdied.png|thumb|left|250px|Mon Mothma was the first chancellor of the New Republic.]]
After the [[death]] of [[Emperor]] Palpatine during the [[Battle of Endor]], the Rebel Alliance formed the New Republic and the Galactic Senate was reconvened on Mothma's [[homeworld]] of [[Chandrila]]. Although Mothma was elected as first chancellor of the New Republic,<ref name="Aftermath" /> she technically succeeded Palpatine as chancellor via the charter of chancellor which included the emergency powers that had once been given to her predecessor during the Clone Wars. However, it was her intention to do away with those powers, believing them to be a poison to [[democracy]].<ref name="TSWB" /> In a short time after being elected,<ref name="Aftermath" /> Mothma then eliminated the emergency powers granted to her by the chancellery's charter.<ref name="TFA VD" /> Mothma also planned to propose a massive military disarmament once the [[Galactic Civil War]] came to end, hoping to cut the size of the New Republic Defense Force by ninety percent. While the other ten percent would go towards training and supporting local militias. She proposed to put these ideas on the agenda before the New Republic Senate.<ref name="Aftermath" />

With the end of the war and the signing of the [[Galactic Concordance]], the peace treaty with the Empire, saw the achievement of that proposal through the [[Military Disarmament Act]].<ref name="TFA VD" /> Despite some debate over Coruscant's future role within the New Republic,<ref name="Rise and Fall" /> it was ultimately decided that the Galactic Senate would convene amongst member [[Planet|worlds]] on a rotational basis,<ref name="TFA VD" /> as part of Chancellor Monthma's further reforms,<ref name="Hosnian Prime Databank">{{Databank|hosnian-prime|Hosnian Prime}}</ref> doing much to convince [[star system]]s that the New Republic would be different from its predecessor governments.<ref name="TFA VD" /> Nevertheless, Coruscant would retain some government operations as it was already designed to handle and administer the galaxy's infrastructure.<ref name="Rise and Fall" />

===Abolishment attempt===
{{Main|First Senator}}
{{Quote|I hereby propose the abolition of the title ''chancellor''. In its stead, we will elect a 'First Senator'—and that First Senator will be given ''real'' authority over economic and military matters. Our troops and politicians will be answerable again. The Senate will have to cooperate. And we can finally move the New Republic forward!|Lady Carise Sindian|<ref name="Bloodline" />}}
[[File:First_Senator_Leia_poster.png|thumb|right|250px|The New Republic Senate considered replacing the title of chancellor with a new office known as First Senator.]]
Chancellor Mothma was credited with forging a political consensus during her term in office that allowed the New Republic to establish itself as a lasting power. However, after her term in office ended in sometime after<ref name="Bloodline" /> [[9 ABY]],<ref name="9 ABY date">The events of {{Ahsoka|Part Three: Time to Fly}} which features [[Mon Mothma]] still acting as Chancellor of the [[New Republic]], can be dated to [[9 ABY]] per the reasoning [[Template:AhsokaSeriesDate|here]].</ref> her successors failed to create that same political consensus, a consensus that Senator [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] credited to her charisma as a leader. By [[28 ABY]], two political factions&mdash;the [[Centrists]] and the [[Populists]]&mdash;had emerged with divergent views on the role of the central government and the power of the executive. [[Lady]] [[Carise Sindian]], a Centrist, eventually proposed the abolition of the office of the chancellor and a redrafting of the Republic's constitution to create a new position: [[First Senator]], which she proposed would have strong authority over economics and the military. A fierce debate emerged amongst those who favored a strong central authority and those who worried that a position like First Senator would lead to the rise of another emperor.<ref name="Bloodline" />

Senator Organa became a leading candidate for the role of First Senator, despite her reservations about the creation of the office. Her candidacy was derailed, however, after it was revealed by her political enemies, including Senator [[Ransolm Casterfo]] and Lady Carise, that she was the daughter of the late [[Sith Lord]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]]. Senator [[Tai-Lin Garr]] replaced her as the populist candidate, but Garr [[Tai-Lin Garr's assassination|was]] soon [[assassin]]ated. The vote to abolish the role of chancellor was then delayed and both parties agreed that the election for First Senator should be postponed indefinitely.<ref name="Bloodline" />

===Lanever Villecham===
{{Quote|Not realising that the ideology that had once produced stormtroopers armor was still producing stormtroopers. Chancellor Lanever Villecham resolutely refused to heed the warnings from the likes of General Leia Organa as to what was about to happen.|Beaumont Kin, The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire|<ref name="Rise and Fall" />}}
[[File:Korr_Sella_final_moments.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Lanever Villecham pursued a policy of appeasement with the First Order, which ultimately backfired.]]
In [[32 ABY]],<ref name="32 ABY date">{{Databank|chancellor-villecham|Chancellor Villecham}} states that [[Lanever Villecham]] became Chancellor of the [[New Republic]] two years before the [[Attack on Tuanul]], which corresponds to [[32 ABY]] per ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''.</ref> senator [[Lanever Villecham]] of the [[Tarsunt system]] was elected chancellor<ref name="Databank Villecham">{{Databank|chancellor-villecham|Chancellor Villecham}}</ref> as a strong believer in the peace initiatives of the New Republic and continued to pursue peace with the [[First Order]] during the [[Cold War]] so long as they followed the dictates of the Galactic Concordance. He instead pursued improved trade relations with the neutral worlds of the [[Trans-Hydian Borderlands]], as they had been disaffected from the Republic for [[Standard decade|decades]]. Villecham also had to contend with a private military force, the [[Resistance]], led by [[general]] Leia Organa, that pursued evidence that the First Order was violating the Galactic Concordance.<ref name="TFA VD" />

A [[34 ABY|year later]], Organa dispatched an envoy to the then [[capital]] of [[Hosnian Prime]], [[Commander]] [[Korr Sella]] to argue for a military build-up against the First Order with the chancellor on her behalf, as she thought she would never get out of the [[Hosnian system]] alive if she went, but by then it was too late,<ref name="TFA VD" /> with her ultimately proven right when the First Order used its [[superweapon]], [[Starkiller Base]], to target the Republic. It [[Hosnian Cataclysm|destroyed]] Hosnian Prime, killing chancellor Villecham and the rest of the star system's population.<ref name="Episode VII">{{Film|VII}}</ref>

==Protection==
{{Main|Senate Guard (New Republic)}}
The [[Senate Guard (New Republic)|Senate Guard]] was a [[Law enforcement agency|security force]] entrusted with the safety of the Galactic Senate.<ref name="Life Debt" /> In addition to to protecting members of the Senate, the Guard could also be deployed for crowd control and security purposes.<ref name="Empire's End" />

